  "notes": "120-123 address the Prophet ﷺ: no plate on him; a book for «الحق» (the revelation coming to him), geometric for «ولله غيب السماوات والأرض وإليه يرجع الأمر كله» (it leaves before «فاعبده»; nothing on the negated «بغافل»). The unseen is never drawn. 121-122 are a threat: Al-Muyassar's «وفي هذا تهديد ووعيد لهم». Cut: «أولو العزم من الرسل» (46:35) and «يميز الخبيث من الطيب» (3:179). The plan's «تثبيت الفؤاد» restated the verse. STAGING v4: c1 (120) stays ambient (light, no threat): it is addressed to the Prophet himself (the stories are told to make firm your heart), so nothing is staged; params.quiet over 120:1-14; a book plate for the truth that came to you (120:14-17). c2 (121-122): say to those who do not believe (the Prophet is told to say it): the people addressed, three faceless men in dark robes in a town by day, the camera only: nobody speaks, points or turns, no pan drifts to an empty side, no plate starts on 121:1; the camera on them (121:3, 122:2) and wide for we are working (121:8); an hourglass for wait (122:1-3, Al-Muyassar: a threat). c3 (123) stays ambient (geometric): the unseen of the heavens and the earth belongs to Allah and the command to the Prophet to worship Him and rely on Him (his own worship is never staged); params.quiet over all of 123; geometric for the unseen and the return of all matters to Him (123:1-8), gone before the command (123:9); nothing on the negated not unaware (123:12-16). Cover: the book plate under the light (why the stories are told)."
